From a5447aa81f9d5f99f3d96aff005df239e59648e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:33:13 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/31] kcm_recentFiles: what to remember first, History
 section last; application list and QML engine started after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form (QtWidgets kept, docs/page-design.md §8: QFormLayout, bold section labels, no frames). Config keys, kcfg,
D-Bus DeleteRecentStats calls and the "Forget ..." menu unchanged. Not built yet.

Moved / renamed:
- Order by use: "Remember opened documents" (all / none / only for specific applications + the application list and
  "Exclude applications not on the list") is first; the rarer "History" section follows: "Keep history:" and the Clear History
  menu button, now on its own row and labelled "Clear History…" because it opens a menu (kcm_recentFiles/whatToRemember,
  keepHistoryFor, buttonClearRecentHistory).
- The label next to the radios became a bold section label above them; the form layout only holds the History rows
  (buddy set on "Keep history:").
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006 (order by use), HIG-057 (noun section titles), ellipsis on buttons that open a menu.

Speed causes (kcms/recentFiles): (1) ExcludedApplicationsModel::load() opened the activity SQLite database and called
KService::serviceByDesktopName per application inside load(); it now runs from QTimer::singleShot(0) so the page paints
first and the list fills in (the model resets/inserts rows itself). (2) QQuickWidget::setSource (QML engine start for the
list) is deferred the same way. After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Unconfirmed: a Qt .ui XML comment before a widget inside <item> is ignored by uic (standard XML comment; not compiled).
Not done: porting to QML (large; the model needs a QObject-owned config); duplicate with kcm_activities isPrivate left as is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
